---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Transformation — INNOVA Applied Innovation & Technology"
  description="INNOVA maps business processes, prioritizes high-value automation opportunities and builds the appropriate AI or software architecture around measurable outcomes."
  canonicalURL="https://innovaconsult.ca/ai-transformation"
>
  <Header active="ai" />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">INNOVA</a> / Capability / AI Transformation</p>
        <p class="eyebrow">Applied AI</p>
        <h1 class="display">AI transformation is not buying AI tools. <span class="gradient-text">It is redesigning how work happens.</span></h1>
        <p class="kicker">We start with the operating model, not the model provider. The goal is to find where automation creates measurable value and then use the simplest architecture that can deliver it reliably.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell operating-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">INNOVA approach</p><h2 class="h2">A disciplined path from process to production.</h2><p class="kicker">Disconnected pilots create tool sprawl. We use one implementation chain with governance and measurement built through it.</p></div>
        <div class="process">
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">01</span><strong>Process Discovery</strong><span>How work happens now</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">02</span><strong>Opportunity Mapping</strong><span>Where value exists</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">03</span><strong>Prioritization</strong><span>Value vs complexity</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">04</span><strong>Solution Architecture</strong><span>Choose the right system</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">05</span><strong>Implementation</strong><span>Build & integrate</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">06</span><strong>Governance</strong><span>Control risk</span></div>
          <div class="process-row"><span class="num">07</span><strong>Measurement</strong><span>Prove the outcome</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p><h2 class="h2">AI where it fits. Conventional software where it does not.</h2></div><p class="kicker">We do not force AI into deterministic workflows. Architecture should reflect uncertainty, data quality, approval requirements and the cost of failure.</p></div>
        <div class="domain-grid">
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 01</small><h3>Deterministic software</h3><p>For rules, calculations and workflows that should behave the same way every time.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 02</small><h3>Conventional automation</h3><p>For repetitive system-to-system actions with stable inputs and clear triggers.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 03</small><h3>AI assistant</h3><p>For human-led workflows that benefit from drafting, analysis, retrieval or decision support.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 04</small><h3>AI agent</h3><p>For bounded workflows where software can plan, use tools and complete actions under controls.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 05</small><h3>Multi-agent system</h3><p>For decomposable workflows requiring specialized roles, checks or parallel execution.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 06</small><h3>Human-in-the-loop</h3><p>For sensitive operations where human approval remains part of the control architecture.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Option 07</small><h3>Hybrid</h3><p>For real operational environments that combine deterministic systems, AI and human judgment.</p></article>
          <article class="domain"><small>Always</small><h3>Governance layer</h3><p>Privacy, permissions, auditability, data handling, model risk and escalation paths.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell product-panel">
        <span class="product-status">INNOVA product</span>
        <h2 class="product-title">Turn process discovery into an automation portfolio.</h2>
        <p class="product-copy">INNOVA AI Workflow OS is the product layer behind this methodology — mapping operations, scoring opportunities, designing implementation paths and tracking impact.</p>
        <a class="button button-dark button-arrow" href="/workflow-os">Explore Workflow OS</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell split">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Outcomes</p><h2 class="h2">Measure operations, not AI theatre.</h2></div>
        <div class="list-panel">
          <div class="list-item"><strong>Reduced cycle time</strong><p>Move work through the organization faster without losing control.</p></div>
          <div class="list-item"><strong>Fewer repetitive tasks</strong><p>Remove manual work where automation is technically and economically justified.</p></div>
          <div class="list-item"><strong>Lower operating cost</strong><p>Connect implementation spend to a visible operational baseline.</p></div>
          <div class="list-item"><strong>Better decision quality</strong><p>Use AI where information synthesis and structured decision support create value.</p></div>
          <div class="list-item"><strong>Higher process visibility</strong><p>Make workflows, ownership, exceptions and bottlenecks more observable.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
